research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1613-[L1] The limit condition: $\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = P$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x$ in the domain of $h$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|h(x) - P| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1614-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1615-[L2] Absolute value: $|u| \ge 0$; $|u| = 0$ if and only if $u = 0$; $|uv| = |u|\,|v|$; and $|{-u}| = |u|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1616-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1617-[L3] Triangle inequality: $|u + v| \le |u| + |v|$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1618-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1619-[L4] Order and field arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: adding two strict inequalities ([[lem-of-add-order]]); for $t > 0$, $u < v$ is equivalent to $ut < vt$, and $0 \le u \le v$ with $0 \le s \le t$ gives $us \le vt$ ([[lem-of-sign-rules]]); positive elements have positive inverses and $0 < a < b$ gives $0 < 1/b < 1/a$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]]); $0 < 1$ ([[cor-of-one-positive]]), so $2 > 0$ and $t/2 > 0$ for $t > 0$; inverses and the field identities ([[def-field]]); trichotomy and totality, so of finitely many positive reals the smallest is positive ([[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1620-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md:1621:[L5] Local boundedness: there are a real $\delta_0 > 0$ and a real $K \ge 0$ with $|f(x)| \le K$ for every $x \in A$ satisfying $0 < |x - c| < \delta_0$ ([[lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1622-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1623-[L6] Sign preservation: if $M \ne 0$ there is a real $\delta_s > 0$ with $|g(x)| > |M|/2 > 0$ for every $x \in A$ satisfying $0 < |x - c| < \delta_s$, and $c$ is a limit point of $A_0$ ([[lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1624-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1625-[L7] Restriction: if $B \subseteq A$ has $c$ as a limit point and $\lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L$, then $\lim_{x \to c} f|_B(x) = L$ (claim 2 of [[lem-limit-is-local]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1626-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-sign-preservation-near-a-limit.prompt.md-1627-[L8] Neighbourhoods ([[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
