research/audit/wave7-preserved-refuters/ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function--5d60cf0531f6e824.prompt.md-1978-[L1] The limit condition: $\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = P$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x$ in the domain of $h$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|h(x) - P| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
