research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-a6-retry5-ex-x-times-psi-tends-to-zero.prompt.md-1958-[L1] The limit condition: $\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = P$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x$ in the domain of $h$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|h(x) - P| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
