research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1978-[L1] The limit condition: $\lim_{x \to c} h(x) = P$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x$ in the domain of $h$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|h(x) - P| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1979-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1980-[L2] Absolute value: $|u| \ge 0$; $|u| = 0$ if and only if $u = 0$; $|uv| = |u|\,|v|$; and $|{-u}| = |u|$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1981-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1982-[L3] Triangle inequality: $|u + v| \le |u| + |v|$ ([[lem-of-triangle-inequality]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1983-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1984-[L4] Order and field arithmetic in $\mathbb{R}$: adding two strict inequalities ([[lem-of-add-order]]); for $t > 0$, $u < v$ is equivalent to $ut < vt$, and $0 \le u \le v$ with $0 \le s \le t$ gives $us \le vt$ ([[lem-of-sign-rules]]); positive elements have positive inverses and $0 < a < b$ gives $0 < 1/b < 1/a$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]]); $0 < 1$ ([[cor-of-one-positive]]), so $2 > 0$ and $t/2 > 0$ for $t > 0$; inverses and the field identities ([[def-field]]); trichotomy and totality, so of finitely many positive reals the smallest is positive ([[def-ordered-field]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-ex-limit-at-infinity-of-a-rational-function.prompt.md-1985-
