research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1085-## Statement
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1086-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1087-**False claim:** let $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$, let $c$ be a limit point of $A$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1088-([[def-limit-point-r]]) and let $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$ have a limit at $c$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1089-([[def-function-limit]]). Then $f$ is bounded on $A$, that is, the image $f(A)$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1090-is a bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-bounded-set]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1091-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1092-**What is true is the local statement**,
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md:1093:[[lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness]]: there is a *radius* $\delta > 0$ such
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1094-that $f$ is bounded on $A \cap N^{*}_{\delta}(c)$. The radius is produced by the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1095-limit condition at the single tolerance $\varepsilon = 1$, and it carries no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1096-information whatever about the values of $f$ far from $c$, which the limit
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1097-condition never constrains.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1098-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1099-The witness below is $f(x) = 1/x$ on $(0, \infty)$ at the point $c = 1$: the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1100-limit there is $1$, and $f$ is bounded near $1$, while on the whole domain
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1101-$f$ takes values above every real.
--
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1125-1.1 The point $1$ lies in $A = (0,\infty)$ and is a limit point of $A$: given a real $\varepsilon > 0$, let $\rho$ be the smaller of $\varepsilon$ and $1$, so $\rho > 0$; then $1 + \rho/2 > 1 > 0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $0 < |(1 + \rho/2) - 1| = \rho/2 < \varepsilon$. [L2, L3, L5]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1126-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1127-1.2 $f$ is well defined on $A$: every $x \in A$ has $x > 0$, hence $x \ne 0$ and $x^{-1}$ exists, with $x^{-1} > 0$. [L4, L7]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1128-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1129-2.1 The limit of $f$ at $1$ exists and equals $1$. Let $\varepsilon > 0$ be an arbitrary real and let $\delta$ be the smaller of $1/2$ and $\varepsilon/2$, so $\delta > 0$. For $x \in A$ with $0 < |x - 1| < \delta$ we get $x > 1 - 1/2 = 1/2 > 0$, hence $0 < 1/x < 2$ by [L4]; and $|1/x - 1| = |(1 - x)/x| = |x - 1| \cdot (1/x) < \delta \cdot 2 \le \varepsilon$. [step 1.1, step 1.2, L1, L3, L4, L5]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1130-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1131-2.2 The image $f(A)$ has no upper bound. Let $M$ be an arbitrary real; by [L6] fix a natural $n \ge 1$ with $M < n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}}$, and note $n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}} > 0$. Then $x := (n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}})^{-1}$ satisfies $x > 0$, so $x \in A$, and $f(x) = x^{-1} = n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}} > M$. So no real bounds $f(A)$ above, and $f(A)$ is not bounded. [step 1.2, L4, L6, L7]
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1132-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md:1133:3.1 So $f$ has a limit at the limit point $c = 1$ of its domain and is unbounded on that domain: the claim is false, while [[lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness]] remains true and gives boundedness on $A \cap N^{*}_{1/2}(1)$, where indeed $0 < f(x) < 2$ by step 2.1. [step 2.1, step 2.2, L7] ∎
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1134-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1135-## Remarks
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1136-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1137-- **The limit hypothesis is entirely local and the conclusion asked for is global**, so no argument could bridge them. The witness makes that concrete by putting the unbounded behaviour at the *other* end of the domain, arbitrarily far from $c$ in the only sense available here.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1138-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1139-- **The sequential analogue is true**, and that contrast is worth noting: a convergent sequence *is* bounded ([[lem-convergent-implies-bounded]]), because a sequence has only finitely many terms outside any tail, and finitely many reals are bounded. A function has no such structure: the part of $A$ outside a punctured neighbourhood of $c$ can be infinite and can carry arbitrary values.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1140-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.prompt.md-1141-- **A bounded version does hold with an extra hypothesis**: if $A$ is itself contained in a punctured neighbourhood of $c$ on which the limit estimate applies, then local and global boundedness coincide. That is a hypothesis on the domain, not a theorem about limits.
--
