research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-125-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-126-**False claim:** let $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$, let $c$ be a limit point of $A$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-127-([[def-limit-point-r]]) and let $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$ have a limit at $c$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-128-([[def-function-limit]]). Then $f$ is bounded on $A$, that is, the image $f(A)$
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-129-is a bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-bounded-set]]).
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-130-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-131-**What is true is the local statement**,
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md:132:[[lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness]]: there is a *radius* $\delta > 0$ such
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-133-that $f$ is bounded on $A \cap N^{*}_{\delta}(c)$. The radius is produced by the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-134-limit condition at the single tolerance $\varepsilon = 1$, and it carries no
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-135-information whatever about the values of $f$ far from $c$, which the limit
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-136-condition never constrains.
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-137-
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-138-The witness below is $f(x) = 1/x$ on $(0, \infty)$ at the point $c = 1$: the
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-139-limit there is $1$, and $f$ is bounded near $1$, while on the whole domain
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-refuter-fs-limit-exists-implies-bounded-on-the-domain.prompt.md-140-$f$ takes values above every real.
