research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-completeness-limits.provenance.jsonl-44-{"id":"thm-two-sided-limit-iff-both-one-sided","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-sided_limit","https://www.jirka.org/ra/html/sec_limoffunc.html"],"rationale":"Lebl, Proposition 3.1.17, states exactly the local hypotheses that c is a cluster point of both one-sided restrictions and concludes that the two-sided limit equals L iff both one-sided limits equal L; it also gives the equal-limits consequence. The local proof is independently expanded.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
